  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\nTech is driving the bus this Monday morning with NASDAQ up 1.99% and XLK leading sectors at +2.89%. VIX cooling off to 24.62 suggests Friday's selling pressure is easing, but we're still in elevated vol territory above the 20 handle.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Consumer Inflation Expectations (3:00 PM)</strong> - High impact data that could shift Fed expectations</li>\n<li><strong>Red Sea Shipping Tensions</strong> - Houthi threats escalating, watch energy names and shipping stocks</li>\n<li><strong>Treasury Bill Auctions</strong> - 3M and 6M auctions at 3:30 PM will signal funding demand</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Momentum</strong> - XLK gap up needs follow-through volume to stick</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Middle East tensions heating up with Red Sea shipping threats and Iran sanctions. Oil market could get legs if this escalates further.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\nRisk-on rotation back into growth with Tech, Small Caps (IWM +1.36%) and Energy leading. Defensive sectors getting sold - Utilities down 1.13%, Real Estate off 1.03%. Classic growth over value setup if this holds.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Tech breakout with VIX declining suggests institutional buying returning. Small cap strength indicates risk appetite broadening beyond mega caps.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>VIX still elevated above 24 and geopolitical risks rising. Friday's late-day selling shows institutions are quick to hit exits on any weakness.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $745</strong> - Key resistance from last week's highs, needs to clear for continuation</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $720</strong> - Round number resistance, watch for algorithm selling</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 22.50</strong> - Support level, break below signals vol compression trade</li>\n<li><strong>XLK $250</strong> - Sector ETF testing prior highs, failure here kills the tech rally</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
